  "id": "PALOMAR-2026-10-07-000001-v1",
  "title": "A counterexample to Vaught's conjecture for infinitary logic",
  "abstract": "There is a counterexample to Vaught's conjecture for L_{omega_1,omega}. This formalization is based on an unpublished draft by Robin Knight. It constructs a sentence in a countable relational language with exactly aleph-one isomorphism classes of countable models and no nonempty perfect set of pairwise nonisomorphic model codes. This is not a counterexample to the first-order Vaught conjecture.",
